/-!
# Rank-one and odd-extension refinements on the original natural plane

The binary rank-one carrier gives equality at the second normalizer.
Proper odd prime and prime-square embeddings force field four; the
latter also forces PSL₂(25). The source exceptional primes, and thirteen
in PSL₂(25), do not divide any binary GL of dimension at most six.
The image of an action kernel in the simple two-core quotient is either
trivial or full. The first case contradicts these order divisors; the
second gives a two-group action image, killed by perfectness. Thus the
literal natural L₂ action excludes every proper odd rank-one row.

An elementary p-kernel extension of SL₂(p) is generated by p-elements.
That generation lifts through the containing component's two-core by
perfectness, so the same full-plane bound excludes this source row.
Both extension rows also give the first-index refinement with field four
derived from their actual smaller section. The nilpotent SL₂(5) extension
still requires its separate second-index signalizer argument.

The rank-one equality feeds actual Source.UniqueNoncentralComponent:
at field four the central-kernel action argument controls all of V₂;
in arbitrary degree the preceding full-radical action gives that control.
All statements retain C_V(L). The natural quotient, kernel and radical
premises belong to qt-d-1222-natural-flag-cartan, with final discharge by
qt-d-1222-natural-local-geometry. The relative-components owner retains
the remaining carrier branches and field-four triangle.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith 11.0.3, 11.1.1--11.1.3 and G.7.1,
printed pp.760--765,347, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004.
-/

